---
name: reflection
description: >
  A persona's own successful action, recorded as a first-person observation
  memory (backend/cognition.py, remember_outcome). The command verb
  selects the phrasing: arriving somewhere, doing an activity, drinking
  (with a sick variant for contaminated water, #300), idling (if chosen
  as a settled-wait #614), agent-initiated talk_to (with an optional topic,
  #614), studying or eating (#615), checking out or reading a library book
  (#616, the read phrasing quoting the book's content when there is any),
  or a quoted fallback for any other command.
  A failed/blocked attempt (#636) is recorded instead as
  I tried to "<command>" but it didn't work: <reason> -- the failed flag
  overrides the verb-selected phrasing. The reason clause is dropped when
  the parser left no message (run_simulation then passes the command back as
  the reason, so "reason == command" reads as "no reason available").
  A timed-out decide (#758) is recorded as
  I was thinking about what to do at <place> but couldn't decide in time.
  -- there is no command on that path (nothing was chosen), so the
  timed_out flag overrides everything else; the "at <place>" clause is
  dropped when the agent stands nowhere.
  The memory's importance is chosen in Python (it is data, not text), so
  only the wording lives here.
inputs:
  verb:
    type: string
    description: The command verb -- "travel", "perform", "drink", "boil", "wait", "talk_to", "study", "eat", "check_out_book", "read", or anything else.
  person:
    type: string
    description: Who was talked to (used when verb == "talk_to").
  location:
    type: string
    description: The place arrived at (used when verb == "travel").
  activity:
    type: string
    description: What the persona did, as a gerund phrase (used when verb == "perform"); rendered past tense ("I was <activity>.", #851) -- the memory records a finished action, and #826's recent_actions block replays it under a "how long ago" prefix.
  item:
    type: string
    description: What was drunk (verb == "drink"), eaten (verb == "eat"), checked out, or read (verb == "check_out_book" or "read").
  content:
    type: string
    description: The book's read_text, quoted in the read memory (verb == "read"; empty when the thing carried no text).
  sick:
    type: boolean
    description: Whether this drink just sickened the persona (verb == "drink").
  recovered:
    type: boolean
    description: Whether this drink just cured the persona's sickness (verb == "drink", #300).
  topic:
    type: string
    description: What was brought up (verb == "talk_to") or studied (verb == "study"); may be empty.
  minutes:
    type: integer
    description: How many in-game minutes the study took (verb == "study", #615).
  command:
    type: string
    description: The raw command, quoted verbatim in the fallback (any other verb).
  failed:
    type: boolean
    description: Whether this records a failed/blocked attempt (#636); selects the failure phrasing, overriding verb.
  reason:
    type: string
    description: The parser's fail message for the blocked attempt (verb-agnostic; used when failed is true, #636).
  timed_out:
    type: boolean
    description: Whether this records a decide that blew its wall-clock budget (#758); overrides every other phrasing (a timeout has no command or verb).
  place:
    type: string
    description: Where the persona stood while deciding (used when timed_out is true, #758); empty when it stands nowhere.
sample:
  verb: drink
  location: ""
  activity: ""
  item: cup of murky water
  sick: true
  recovered: false
  command: ""
---
{%- if timed_out and place -%}
I was thinking about what to do at {{ place }} but couldn't decide in time.
{%- elif timed_out -%}
I was thinking about what to do but couldn't decide in time.
{%- elif failed and reason and reason != command -%}
I tried to "{{ command }}" but it didn't work: {{ reason }}
{%- elif failed -%}
I tried to "{{ command }}" but it didn't work.
{%- elif verb == "travel" -%}
I traveled to {{ location }}.
{%- elif verb == "perform" -%}
I was {{ activity }}.
{%- elif verb == "drink" and sick -%}
I drank the {{ item }} and now I feel terribly sick.
{%- elif verb == "drink" and recovered -%}
I drank the {{ item }}, and the sickness has finally passed -- I feel much better.
{%- elif verb == "drink" -%}
I drank the {{ item }}.
{%- elif verb == "boil" -%}
I boiled the water to make it safe to drink.
{%- elif verb == "wait" -%}
I waited; nothing needed doing.
{%- elif verb == "talk_to" and topic -%}
I went to talk to {{ person }} about {{ topic }}.
{%- elif verb == "talk_to" -%}
I went to talk to {{ person }}.
{%- elif verb == "study" and topic -%}
I studied {{ topic }} for {{ minutes }} minutes.
{%- elif verb == "study" -%}
I studied for {{ minutes }} minutes.
{%- elif verb == "eat" -%}
I ate the {{ item }}.
{%- elif verb == "check_out_book" -%}
I checked out {{ item }} from the library.
{%- elif verb == "read" and content -%}
I read {{ item }}. It said: "{{ content }}"
{%- elif verb == "read" -%}
I read {{ item }}.
{%- else -%}
I did "{{ command }}".
{%- endif -%}
